  "_note": "Wrist-aware reachability companion to prostate_access_feasibility.py. The instrument is modelled as the polyline port -> W -> target; the shaft AND the distal wrist+jaw segment are clearance-checked (centre ray on both segments, 6 mm radius in arc length excluding the first 20 mm and the last 12 mm of arc). At theta = 0 this is exactly the original straight-shaft model. Conservative (a) = max |wrist pitch| only; optimistic (b) = acos(cos pmax * cos ymax). Sampled bend directions are nominal about the port->target line; the ACCEPTED bend is the angle between the actual shaft direction port->W and the distal direction, verified <= theta_max. Exploratory geometric feasibility only; no deformation, no clinical claim.",
